    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="12c1b5c3-b33a-5c8a-86a5-3556edd5706a" activityNameId="3f69d73a-b645-5dce-a6c7-7f15712d6563" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, ventilator unit 6700 m3/h, modular, w. filter, without silencer, Device</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, ventilator unit 6700 m3/h, modular, w. filter, without silencer, Device
Disposal of a ventilator unit for a air handling unit with 6700 m3/h nominal air flow rate (at 2 m/s air speed in cross section of air filter or heat exchanger), component weight: 435 kg, total weight: 571 kg/Unit, including average components for controls, inverter and electric control cabinet, material for 20 filter replacements (once a year for 20 years lifetime). The ventilator of the air handling unit includes a frame construction, one radial belt drive fan, multi-leaf damper. No heat recovery, heating and/or cooling elements, humidifier, air-mixing plenum and silencer included. The frame construction made of aluminium-profiles, casing made of hot-dip galvanized and powder coated steel sheets insulated with polyurethane foam.
Transport to dismantling facilities, machines for handling in sorting plant, electricity demand for sorting plant, final disposal of waste material. Cut-off to recycling for metals.
Location:  Specific to the technology mix encountered in sorting plants in Switzerland.
Technology: Disposal to a sorting plant assumed. Metal pieces, copper in cables and electronic devices are recycled, plastic parts are incinerated, inert wastes (e.g. rock wool) are landfilled.
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2013. Disposal technology mix as used in late 1990ies
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Waste-specific calculation based on production input data
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_e1ca0767-af7c-4eac-a7e8-7f35824b671e.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
